    <string name="identities_gen_x25519_body">Creates a fresh age X25519 key pair, stored in your vault.</string>
    <string name="identities_gen_hybrid_body">Creates a fresh MLKEM768-X25519 hybrid key pair, safe against future quantum computers and compatible with age 1.3.0 and later. Files encrypted to it can use only quantum-safe recipients (it can\'t be mixed with a classical key).</string>
    <string name="identities_gen_ssh_body">Creates a fresh SSH Ed25519 key pair, stored in your vault. Use it to sign files (including encrypt-and-sign). It can also receive files as an ssh-ed25519 recipient.</string>
    <string name="identities_gen_hardware_body">Creates a non-exportable P-256 key in this device\'s secure hardware (StrongBox or TEE). It can sign but not decrypt.</string>
    <string name="identities_require_unlock_sign">Require biometric or device unlock to sign</string>
    <string name="identities_error_hardware_create">Couldn\'t create the hardware key.</string>
    <string name="identities_gen_hardware_decrypt_body">Creates a P-256 key inside this device\'s secure hardware (StrongBox or TEE). Files are encrypted to it as usual, including from the age command line (1.3 or later), and only this phone can open them.</string>
    <string name="identities_no_backup_detail">This key can\'t be exported, moved to another device, or backed up. If this phone is lost, reset, or broken, anything encrypted only to this key is gone. Encrypt important files to a second recipient as well.</string>
    <string name="identities_hardware_decrypt_pq_switch">Quantum-safe (adds ML-KEM-768)</string>
    <string name="identities_hardware_decrypt_pq_detail">age1tagpq1… recipient. The ML-KEM half is held in your vault, the P-256 half in hardware; both are needed to decrypt. A file encrypted to it can only include other quantum-safe recipients.</string>
    <string name="identities_hardware_decrypt_classic_detail">age1tag1… recipient. Works alongside any other recipient type.</string>
    <string name="identities_require_unlock_decrypt">Require biometric or device unlock to decrypt</string>
    <string name="identities_screen_lock_warning">Android deletes keys like this if you ever remove the device\'s screen lock. Only turn this on if you\'ll keep a screen lock set.</string>
    <string name="identities_gen_security_body">Enrolls a FIDO security key (YubiKey, Token2) as a signing identity over NFC. The private key never leaves the security key.</string>
